# Keys that sign warden's release manifests, in the format of ssh-keygen -Y verify -f
# (see "ALLOWED SIGNERS" in ssh-keygen(1)). A copy of the warden-release keys in
# https://github.com/pecheriere/warden/blob/main/docs/release-signers, kept here so
# that a formula is checked against keys this repository's own review approved, not
# against whatever the release's tag says. Change it in step with warden's list.
# Every key is listed under the identity warden-release, which is what
# scripts/formula.py checks. warden's list keeps the maintainer's older key under the
# maintainer's address, because its release tags verify with that, but a manifest
# signature does not carry a name, so the name here is this repository's choice.
# The maintainer's key, which signed every release up to 0.12.0. Removed once the
# releases signed through warden's broker are out.
warden-release namespaces="warden-release" ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIN5zA+J2lBK+qWdhVBz+3WiucLhgDfWn3Yw0JHZyIhBJ
# The key warden's broker holds and signs releases with, from 0.13.0,
# SHA256:q7ezyVes9zAFsYyAtOqarJZJckRAVSikw9le8ufdSdc.
warden-release namespaces="warden-release" ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIPU8lP0ukIXv5Oi6ozNGvBHVvAzZBNvxxN8NpnCh/t0R
